# Database Conventions

- Every migration has up and down; fully reversible. Migrations are additive
  during transitions; never alter a column type in place. Add a new column,
  backfill, drop the old one in a later migration.
- UUID primary keys via `gen_random_uuid()`, `timestamptz`, snake_case.
- Canonical domain tables are the normalized set (`provision`, `module`,
  `legal_source`, `answer_candidate`, `curated_answer`, plus the operational
  tables). `corpus_chunks` is the embedding layer referencing `provision.id`,
  not a domain table.
- Embeddings are 1024-dimension and local (bge-large-en-v1.5 or
  mxbai-embed-large via Ollama). Do not introduce a 1536 or external
  (text-embedding-3-small) embedding. Store model name and dimension per row.
- Provisions carry `effective_from` / `effective_to` / `status`. Law-as-at-date:
  `effective_from <= :d AND (effective_to IS NULL OR effective_to > :d)`.
- `curated_answer.citation_ids` must be non-empty (CHECK). No citation, no
  promotion.
- Per-service least-privilege roles; the corpus read role is separate from the
  app read-write role. Knowledge tables live in a `knowledge` schema.
- Enable row-level security on `matter` and all matter-scoped tables.
- Graph relationships use Postgres `legal_nodes` / `legal_edges`. Do not add Neo4j.
